  "limitations": [
    "Admission orders the same owner in one EventBus/Engine, not cross-process writers or crash recovery.",
    "Shared queue/pool/CPU/history locks remain shared resources; owner admission metadata, like existing history/settings, is retained for process lifetime. No new total byte/owner quota.",
    "Barriers order earlier publications, not all future producers or snapshot/live recovery; snapshot and unread queries retain independent fallback behavior.",
    "Full/closed queues, failed barriers and selected storage deadlines latch existing volatile fallback until restart, with warnings. Volatile data is not automatically reconciled or restored.",
    "Read/deletion HTTP success can still acknowledge memory only; no new durable acknowledgement or persistence-health wire field was added.",
    "A stage deadline ends application waiting, not necessarily the dispatched database statement, and is not an overall HTTP deadline or proof of rollback.",
    "Known settings/replacement transaction failures are covered; lost commit acknowledgements, process crashes and multi-Engine concurrency are not. Background INSERT retry ambiguity remains.",
    "Equal timestamps have explicit order, but arbitrary timestamp order, database timestamp precision and snapshot/live overlap do not become IDs/cursor replay/exactly-once semantics.",
    "Cold DropNew admission against already-full SQL history and writer lifetime/shutdown draining remain separate inspection targets.",
    "Replacement is a private service helper, not a new HTTP import route. Transactions do not cover the complete publication/HTTP/recovery lifecycle."
  ],
